KNOWNBUG: N5008 [time.duration.nonmember] -- mixed-period duration
operator+ (minutes + seconds) returns nondet: the instantiated operator+
body fails to convert (resolution of the `__cd` common-type alias /
`duration` converting-constructor calls inside it finds no match) and the
failure is swallowed by system-header leniency.  Isolated pieces all work
(same-type operator+, duration_cast, converting ctor, common_type
deduction); only the mixed-period operator+ body is affected.  Found by
feature-sweep defect hunting; g++/clang++ runtime-verified.  Flip to CORE
when the operator+ body converts.
